// src/route-heads.ts — the part of each route that the hook puts in front of the model.
//
// Codex shows a hook's additionalContext whole only while it stays under about 9,832 bytes; past that
// it keeps the first and last 4,916 bytes and drops the middle. So each route sends a short head, in
// order of importance, and names the full route directive and the installed SKILL.md as files the
// model reads when a step needs them. The directive and skill files themselves are unchanged.
//
// `{skill:<name>}` becomes the installed SKILL.md path of that skill (or its catalog name when this
// layout does not ship it), `{skills}` the folder that holds every skill (named once where a table lists
// skills by name) and `{root}` the folder that holds `skills/` and `vendor/`; all are resolved when the
// hook runs.
